        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4e0e9d5f227443d185b285479acc13a5",
      "statement": "Authorization is capability-based: open() computes the caller's effective role and hands use sessions a UseOverseerInterface that implements the entire Overseer interface but throws Unauthorized outside the use allowlist (getUiBundle, connectToGadget against mainline, restricted metadata, presence, plus two inert telemetry subscriptions) — because it implements the interface, a newly-added method fails to compile until a use-role decision is made (default-deny).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/sharing.md#L15-L16",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:35218bee5827f9364f8947813165e8d42594a4fb512c1a239d8aaaa661269d4f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/sharing.md#L28-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a4fe70bdca0b8cf7afd4794204889b6c05513eedb8af02e2013b57fa645df12e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3f8fb6db4ce64808b8f4d845c26a1f9d",
      "statement": "A caller may never grant a role higher than their own effective role — enforced for direct adds and for link copies, where the ceiling is re-checked at copy time because the caller's role may have dropped below the link's since it was created.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/sharing.ts#L434-L471",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:99fb350dda959a03412a6727a776548171fc7604506532cb401021f8637e7cf0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9f671a5ad3c944e3b940d622f5259d2f",
      "statement": "Each collaborator accumulates permission edges explaining how they gained access (a user edge from a specific sharer, or a shareKey edge toward a link with the link's role); multiple edges accumulate and access persists while at least one valid edge remains; the owner is the implicit root at build, never stored in the collaborators table.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/sharing.md#L54-L81",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c38ae64235c74d45484d674113a071d2311f8f6e565d4faffae5d4226bc515bd:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/sharing.ts#L68-L108",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:86a3dd10a957638622c982462ad955330b2cc03e6c09115c39988462f10f1a33:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8649b6eef5314034b7cc9869b36a5f20",
      "statement": "computeEffectiveRoles is the single source of truth: a fixed-point iteration (roles only increase, so it converges) computing each collaborator's maximum role reachable from the owner, where each edge grants min(edge role, sharer's effective role) and a share-link edge's sharer is the link's creator — making share links first-class graph nodes that are transitively revoked when their creator loses access; optional hypothetical inputs (removedUser, removedEdge, revokedLinkId) power the preview methods.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/sharing.ts#L552-L639",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c7ee8b9ebee98d33557925290b0e414a3e093a70cb7d95a86a1dcd7316fc75d6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_515e00ee324145cabb83dbe38547d531",
      "statement": "Share keys: a link is stored as its first key's record (keyed by the key's hash) and copies store only an alias back, so all of a link's keys collapse to one grant; the raw 128-bit key is shown once at mint time and never stored — only its HMAC-SHA-256 with a domain-separation constant — so a database leak does not expose valid keys, and redemption never stores plaintext.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/sharing.md#L38-L44",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:db92ba95db12cbed492e2590f8f0526281ecbd2ff9b761be816b8eb5cd28287c:"
