    {
      "id": "claim_e29afd7a53b640e2b1a1b6940754f383",
      "statement": "Because authorization is checked only at open(), a change that actually removed or downgraded someone restarts the Overseer DO via ctx.abort — after flushing the severed edge with storage.sync() (the abort does not respect the output gate) and delaying ~100ms so the triggering response lands — forcing every client to reconnect and re-run open() against the changed graph; no-op removals do not restart, and prohibitAllSharing can never strand a session because the observation that would set it is blocked when the gadget is already shared.",
      "evidence": [
